        'A train day south of the city, opened by the best breakfast in Fukuoka at a charcoal counter in Ropponmatsu that only serves the morning. Then the great shrine of learning at the peak of its maple colour, the moss garden next door, its woven-wood Starbucks, a flat-bottomed boat down the canals of Yanagawa, and a Friday night that runs yatai to sushi izakaya to Daimyo.',
